# AGENTS.md

Rules for changing {{ .Service.Name }}. They apply to people and coding agents alike.

## Read order

1. [README.md](README.md)
2. [doc/architecture.md](doc/architecture.md)
3. [internal/doc/module-conventions.md](internal/doc/module-conventions.md)
4. The README of the module you are changing
5. [doc/development.md](doc/development.md) before running anything

## Non-negotiable conventions

- A module owns everything under `internal/app/<module>`; other modules call its service, never its repository.
- Layers: resolver / controller (transport only) → service (rules, validation) → repository (SQL only).
  Mappers translate between layers with copier; nothing else converts types.
- Persistent models embed a core-lib base model (`VersionedNamespaceModelIDString` by default).
  Never declare `DeletedAt`, `CreatedBy` and friends yourself.
- Every read filters by namespace (`utility.AppendNamespaceFilterToQuery`) and `deleted_at IS NULL`.
  Every write gets its namespace from the context through the base model hooks.
- List queries go through the entity's column and operator allow-list in the service.
- Migrations are forward-only: never edit one that has run anywhere. Each has a `.down.sql`.
  Every table gets the `log_audit_trigger`.
- No secrets in committed config. They arrive as `APP_*` environment variables or the environment's
  mounted override.
- Generated code (`graphql/generated`) is never edited by hand; run `make gql MODULE=<module>`.
- Hand-written code under `internal/` stays at 100% test coverage (`make cover`).

## Change checklist

- [ ] Migration pair added (`make migrate-new NAME=...`), applied locally, rolled back once, re-applied
- [ ] Model, DTO, repository, service, mappers, resolver / controller updated together
- [ ] `make gql MODULE=<module>` run for each module whose schema changed
- [ ] `make lint` and `make cover` pass
- [ ] Module README updated; this file's module index and README updated if a module was added
- [ ] New GraphQL module added to `scripts/supergraph/supergraph.yaml` and the GitOps router config

